messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Black Mirror" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Karen will share \'Black Mirror\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s break down the problem step by step:.\n\n1.**Identify the key points from the context:**.\n   - "Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.\n   - If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.\n   - If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.\n   - Karen does not download "Black Mirror".\n   - "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.\n   - If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n2.**Analyze the implications of the given information:**.\n   - Since "Black Mirror" is a popular Netflix show (as implied by the context), Karen will binge-watch it.\n   - However, Karen does not download "Black Mirror", which means she does not follow the second condition (if and only if she binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it).\n   - Despite not downloading "Black Mirror", the first condition still holds true because "Black Mirror" is a popular Netflix show.\n\nTherefore, based on the given details, Karen will not share "Black Mirror" with Lisa since the third condition clearly states that sharing does not occur after binge-watching.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
