messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings. If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets. If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age. If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members. If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly. Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Luke is neither a twin nor triplet nor complains often about annoying siblings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Luke is neither a twin nor triplet nor complains often about annoying siblings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s analyze the information step by step:\n\n1.**If people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.**\n   - This implies that if Luke is a twin or triplet, he would have strong bonds with his siblings.\n\n2.**If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.**\n   - This means that if Luke has siblings who are the same age, he would be a twin or triplet.\n\n3.**If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age.**\n   - This suggests that if Luke complains often about annoying siblings, he would have siblings who are the same age.\n\n4.**If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members.**\n   - This indicates that if Luke does not live at home regularly, he would not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\n5.**If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.**\n   - This implies that if Luke spends a lot of time hanging out with and playing with his siblings, he would not live at home regularly.\n\n6.Luke is both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he is neither a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\nGiven these points, let\'s evaluate the statement "Luke is a twin or triplet, and he often complains about annoying siblings":\n\n- According to point 1, if Luke is not a twin or triplet, he would not have strong bonds with his siblings.\n- According to point 2, if Luke does not have siblings who are the same age, he would not be a twin or triplet.\n- According to point 3, if Luke does not complain often about annoying siblings, he would not have siblings who are the same age.\n- According to point 4, if Luke lives at home regularly, he would develop strong bonds with his family members.\n- According to point 5, if Luke does not spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with his siblings, he would live at home regularly.\n\nFrom the above analysis, we can see that if Luke is not a twin or triplet, he would not have strong bonds with his siblings, which supports the statement that he is neither a twin nor triplet nor complains often about annoying siblings. Therefore, the statement is true.\n\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
