messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\n"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show. If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it. If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it. Karen does not download "Black Mirror". "Black Mirror" is a Netflix show. If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Karen will share "Stranger Things" to Lisa.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is true, false, or uncertain, let\'s break down the information provided step by step:\n\n1.**"Stranger Things" is a popular Netflix show.**\n   - This means that according to the context, "Stranger Things" is indeed a popular Netflix show.\n\n2.**If a Netflix show is popular, Karen will binge-watch it.**\n   - Since "Stranger Things" is popular, based on the given rule, Karen will binge-watch "Stranger Things".\n\n3.**If and only if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will download it.**\n   - This means that Karen will download a Netflix show only if she binge-watches it.Therefore, if Karen does not binge-watch "Stranger Things", she will not download it.\n\n4.**Karen does not download "Black Mirror".**\n   - This implies that Karen did not download "Black Mirror".\n\n5.**"Black Mirror" is a Netflix show.**\n   - This is given as fact.\n\n6.**If Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will share it to Lisa.This means that if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will not share it to Lisa. Now, let\'s analyze the situation with "Stranger Things": We know that "Stranger Things" is not popular. Since "Stranger Things" is not popular, Karen will not binge-watch it. However, we also know that Karen does download "Black Mirror", which is another popular Netflix show. The rule states that if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will not download it. Since she did download "Black Mirror", it suggests that she might have binge-watched it as well. But the rule also states that if Karen binge-watches a Netflix show, she will not share it to Lisa. Since we don\'t have any information about whether Karen binge-watched "Stranger Things" or not, we cannot definitively conclude whether she will share it to Lisa. Therefore, based on the information provided, the statement "Karen will share \'Stranger Things\' to Lisa" is certain.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
