messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nOn some Mondays at 8 pm, roses are given out on TV. Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor. Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people. All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows. Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Breaking Bad is on Monday at 8 pm" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s analyze the context step by step:.\n\n1.**Context Analysis:**.\n   - Roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm.\n   - Every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor.\n   - Everything on the Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.\n   - All shows portraying the lives of real people are reality TV shows.\n   - Breaking Bad is not a reality TV show.\n\n2.**Step-by-Step Reasoning:**.\n   - Since roses are given out on TV on some Mondays at 8 pm, and every rose given out on TV is on the Bachelor, it follows that the Bachelor airs on some Mondays at 8 pm.\n   - The Bachelor portrays the lives of real people.Given that the Bachelor is a reality TV show and airs on some Mondays at 8 pm, it is reasonable to conclude that Breaking Bad, which is not a reality TV show, can be on Monday at 8 pm.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
