messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIf people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings. If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets. If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age. If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members. If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly. Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Luke complains often about annoying siblings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>\nTo determine whether the statement "Luke complains often about annoying siblings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s analyze the context step by step:\n\n1.**If people are twins or triplets, then they spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings.**\n   - This implies that if Luke is a twin or triplet, he would likely spend a lot of time with his siblings.\n\n2.**If people have siblings who are the same age, then they are twins or triplets.**\n   - This suggests that if Luke has siblings who are the same age, he might be a twin or triplet.\n\n3.**If people complain often about annoying siblings, then they have siblings who are the same age.**\n   - This indicates that if Luke complains often about annoying siblings, he likely has siblings who are the same age.\n\n4.**If people do not live at home regularly, then they do not develop strong bonds with their family members.**\n   - This implies that if Luke does not live at home regularly, he may not develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\n5.**If people spend a lot of time hanging out with and playing with their siblings, then they often did not live at home regularly.**\n   - This suggests that if Luke spends a lot of time with his siblings, he may not live at home regularly.\n\n6.**Luke is either both a twin or triplet and develops strong bonds with his family members, or he neither is a twin or triplet nor develops strong bonds with his family members.**This does not provide any scenarios for Luke: he is neither a twin nor triplet, and does not have strong bonds with his family.\n\nGiven these points, let\'s evaluate the statement "Luke praises rarely about delightful siblings":\n\n- According to point 3, if Luke praises rarely about delightful siblings, he likely has siblings who are not the same age.\n- According to point 5, if Luke has siblings who are not the same age, he may live at home regularly.\n- According to point 6, if Luke lives at home regularly, he may develop strong bonds with his family members.\n\nHowever, there is no direct information linking Luke\'s praises about siblings to his living situation or his relationship with his family. Therefore, we cannot definitively conclude whether Luke praises rarely about delightful siblings based solely on the provided context.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n**B) Certain**. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
