messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAll mammals are animals. All monkeys are mammals. An animal is either a monkey or a bird. All birds fly. All animals breathe. If something can fly, then it has wings. If Rock is neither a fly nor a bird, then Rock neither flies nor breathes.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or uncertain? Rock does not have wings.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Uncertain', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Rock does not have wings" is true, false, or uncertain based on the given information, let\'s analyze the logical connections step by step:.\n\n1.**All mammals are animals.**.\n   - This means that any mammal is also an animal.\n\n2.**All monkeys are mammals.**.\n   - Therefore, all monkeys are animals.\n\n3.**An animal is either a monkey or a bird.**.\n   - This implies that every animal is either a monkey or a bird.\n\n4.**All birds fly.**.\n   - Since birds fly, they must have wings.\n\n5.**All animals breathe.**.\n   - This means that every animal has the ability to breathe.\n\n6.**If something can fly, then it has wings.**.\n   - This is a logical implication that if an object can fly, it must have wings.If Rock is either a fly or a bird, then Rock both flies and breathes.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
