 the dining hall meals and recipes.**.\n   - This statement presents two alternatives: either ordering takeout frequently or enjoying dining hall meals and recipes.\n\n4.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they are not picky eaters.**.\n   - This statement indicates that enjoying dining hall meals and recipes is a sign of not being picky.\n\n5.**If people enjoy the dining hall meals and recipes, then they spend a lot of their time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.**.\n   - This statement suggests that enjoying dining hall meals and recipes leads to spending time in the dining halls.\n\n6.**If Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition, then Mary is neither picky nor needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.**.\n   - This statement concludes that if Mary works in student jobs and needs money for tuition, she cannot be picky and does not need to earn money for tuition.\n\nNow, let\'s evaluate the statement "Mary is not a picky eater and spends a lot of her time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls":.\n\n- **Mary works in student jobs on campus and needs to earn money to help pay for her college tuition.Based on the information provided, it is uncertain whether Mary is a picky eater or spends a lot of time eating and catching up with friends in the campus dining halls.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
